 It exports `logger.debug/info/warn/error(message, fields?)`. Each call writes one JSON line to stdout with `level`, `message`, any fields and an ISO timestamp. Fields are limited to `string | number | boolean`.
 
-Nothing in `users.ts` or `orders.ts` imports or uses it yet.
+Only `login` in `users.ts` uses it so far. A failed login logs a `warn` with a `reason` (`unknown_account` or `wrong_password`) and, when the account exists, its `userId`. The email is never logged, so failures for unknown accounts cannot be tied to a person. `orders.ts` does not use the logger.
 
 Per `CLAUDE.md`, any logging added to these modules must use this logger and must identify people and orders by `userId` and `orderId` only. It must not log email, name, phone, address, passwords, reset tokens or whole `User` objects. `resetPassword` is the most sensitive spot, because it handles the email and the reset token.
